content.text:
Finding submitted.

**Summary:** The Agreement has no aggregate liability cap. Article 16.5 is only a mutual consequential-damages disclaimer (with carve-outs for the Article 10/16.1/16.2 indemnities and gross negligence/willful misconduct), and Section 17.3(d) merely bars punitive/excess damages in arbitration — so direct liability, including Ono's, is unlimited. That fails the fallback element requiring a mutual 12-months'-fees cap, so I classified it as a **deviation** and proposed a single insertion of new Section 16.7 at the end of Article 16 (numbered to avoid colliding with the existing 16.6 Recalls):

- mutual aggregate cap at the greater of twelve months' fees paid or payable by Ono and USD 1,000,000, measured in the twelve months preceding the claim;
- Excluded Claims (uncapped) for confidentiality, data protection/security, indemnification under Article 10 and Sections 16.1/16.2, gross negligence, willful misconduct, fraud, and IP infringement;
- Ono's payment obligations expressly not damages subject to the cap.

The existing mutual indirect/consequential-damages exclusion in 16.5 was left untouched and mapped as already met.
